.* QTOCPORT: CFGTCP option 4, the port restrictions. WRKPORT has
.* 1=Add and 4=Remove; WRKPORTD shows the list only.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PORTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 5'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=UPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 5'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PCLCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PLOWER CLASS=PORTCL.
:VAR NAME=PUPPER CLASS=UPCL.
:VAR NAME=PPROTO CLASS=PCLCL.
:VAR NAME=PUSER CLASS=NAMECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=PORTS VARS='OPT PLOWER PUPPER PPROTO PUSER'.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.F6=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION='RETURN 18'.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKPORT HELP=HLPPORT KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with TCP/IP Port Restrictions
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=PORTS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No port restrictions)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 101' HELP='WRKPORT/OPTIONS'.1=Add
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 104' HELP='WRKPORT/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKPORT/OPT'.Opt
:LISTGRP COL=RANGE.--Port Range---
:LISTCOL VAR=PLOWER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=8 ATCOL=10 HELP='FLD/PLOWER'.Lower
:LISTCOL VAR=PUPPER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=8 HELP='FLD/PUPPER'.Upper
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL VAR=PPROTO USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/PPROTO'.Protocol
:LISTCOL VAR=PUSER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES ATCOL=43 HELP='FLD/PUSER'.User       Profile
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKPORTD HELP=HLPPORT KEYL=WRKKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with TCP/IP Port Restrictions
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=PORTS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.(No port restrictions)
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='FLD/OPT'.Opt
:LISTGRP COL=RANGE.--Port Range---
:LISTCOL VAR=PLOWER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=8 ATCOL=10 HELP='FLD/PLOWER'.Lower
:LISTCOL VAR=PUPPER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES MAXWIDTH=8 HELP='FLD/PUPPER'.Upper
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL VAR=PPROTO USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/PPROTO'.Protocol
:LISTCOL VAR=PUSER USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES ATCOL=43 HELP='FLD/PUSER'.User       Profile
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPPORT.Work with TCP/IP Port Restrictions - Help
:P.Ports kept for chosen user profiles: a port or range of a protocol
with an entry can be used only by the profiles its entries name. Type 4
next to an entry to remove it; option 1 adds one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Print list
:PD.Print list.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPORT/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PLOWER'.--Port Range--- lower
:P.The --Port Range--- lower of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PUPPER'.--Port Range--- upper
:P.The --Port Range--- upper of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PPROTO'.Protocol
:P.The protocol of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PUSER'.User       Profile
:P.The user Profile of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPORT/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the opt for the entry on the line.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
